        "original_id": "4b89c92a-60c6-5950-89fb-cd9dd3a3f602",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Richard Connell, Berthold Viertel, Paul Muni, Richard Thorpe, Gladys Lehman, Robert Connell\n- Works: Seven Faces, A Friend of Napoleon, The Most Dangerous Game, The Hounds of Zaroff, Bloodlust!, Thrill of a Romance\n- Publications: The Saturday Evening Post, Collier's\n\nFacts:\n- Richard Connell's short fiction \"A Friend of Napoleon\" was published in The Saturday Evening Post on June 30, 1923.\n- Richard Connell's short story \"The Most Dangerous Game,\" also published as \"The Hounds of Zaroff,\" was first published in Collier's on January 19, 1924.\n- Seven Faces was based on Richard Connell's short fiction \"A Friend of Napoleon.\"\n- Seven Faces was directed by Berthold Viertel and starred Paul Muni in his second screen appearance.\n- Richard Connell's best known work was \"The Most Dangerous Game,\" and it was filmed three years after its publication.\n- Bloodlust! is a 1961 American horror thriller film based on Robert Connell's short story \"The Most Dangerous Game.\"\n- Thrill of a Romance was directed by Richard Thorpe and written by Richard Connell and Gladys Lehman.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
